    "title": "What channel is Illinois vs Iowa basketball today? Time, TV schedule to watch Elite 8 game",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 11:39 a.m. ETOne way or another, the Big Ten Conference, which has four teams in the Elite Eight, is guaranteed a spot in the Final Four.Commissioner Tony Pettiti and Co. can thank No. 3 seed Illinois and No. 9 seed Iowa, both out of the South Region, for that particular honor.Stream select March Madness games live with Sling TVBrad Underwood's Fighting Illini have looked physically dominant over their first three March Madness opponents, downing No. 14 seed Pennsylvania, No. 11 seed Virginia Commonwealth and No. 2 seed Houston — at the Toyota Center in Houston — by a combined 56 points, or 18.7 points per game. Each of their victories have come by at least 10 points.Conversely, Iowa enters the matchup having been more battle-tested against No. 8 seed Clemson, No. 1 seed Florida and No. 4 seed Nebraska. The Hawkeyes' six-point wins over the Tigers and Cornhuskers book-end a thrilling 73-72 win over the defending national champion Gators, whom they beat with a last-second 3-pointer from Alvaro Folgueiras.Illinois has already beaten Iowa this season, 75-69 on Jan. 11. Will March 28 see a repeat, or yet another upset?Here's how to watch as Illinois and Iowa face off in an all-Big Ten Elite Eight matchup, including time, TV and streaming information, game odds and more:What channel is Illinois vs Iowa basketball on today in Elite Eight?TV: TBS/truTVStreaming: NCAA March Madness Live | Sling TVIllinois and Iowa basketball's Elite Eight game will broadcast nationally on TBS, with a simulcast on truTV. Kevin Harlan, Stan Van Gundy, Robbie Hummel and Lauren Shehadi will be on the call.Streaming options for the game include the NCAA March Madness Live app (with a valid cable login) or Sling TV, which carries TBS and truTV.Stream Illinois-Iowa live with Sling TVIllinois-Iowa basketball Elite Eight start time todayDate: Saturday, March 28Time: 6:09 p.m. ET | 5:09 p.m. CTLocation: Toyota Center (Houston)The Fighting Illini-Hawkeyes game is scheduled to tip off on March 28 at 6:09 p.m. ET (5:09 p.m. CT) from the Toyota Center in Houston.Illinois vs Iowa picks, predictions, odds in Elite EightOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of 11 a.m. ET on March 28Odds: Illinois (-7.5)Over/under: 137.5Moneyline: Illinois (-325) | Iowa (+260)Predictions:Hawk Central staff: Illinois 73, Iowa 64Adam Duvall, Peoria-Journal Star: Illinois 68, Iowa 62Dave Eminian, Peoria-Journal Star: Illinois 73, Iowa 65Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Gambling involves risk. Please only gamble with funds that you can comfortably afford to lose. While we do our utmost to offer good advice and information we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of gambling. We do our best to make sure all the information that we provide on this site is correct. However, from time to time mistakes will be made and we will not be held liable. Please check any stats or information if you are unsure how accurate they are. No guarantees are made with regards to results or financial gain. All forms of betting carry financial risk and it is up to the individual to make bets with or without the assistance of information provided on this site and we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of following the betting tips provided on this site. Past performances do not guarantee success in the future and betting odds fluctuate from one minute to the next. The material contained on this site is intended to inform, entertain and educate the reader and in no way represents an inducement to gamble legally or illegally or any sort of professional advice.Gannett may earn revenue from sports betting operators for audience referrals to betting services. Sports betting operators have no influence over nor are any such revenues in any way dependent 